namespace Erdos448

/-
# Problem Description

Erdős Problem 448. Let `τ(n)` count the divisors of `n` and `τ⁺(n)` count the number of `k`
such that `n` has a divisor in `[2^k, 2^{k+1})`. Is it true that for all `ε > 0`,
`τ⁺(n) < ε τ(n)` for almost all `n`? `erdos_448` disproves this.

The question appears in [Er79], [ErGr80, p.89] and [Er81h, p.173]; it was refuted by Erdős and
Tenenbaum [ErTe81], who showed the upper density of the exceptional set is bounded below.
Below, `tauPlus n` is `(n.divisors.image (Nat.log 2)).card`, i.e. the number of distinct
dyadic blocks `[2^k, 2^{k+1})` containing a divisor of `n`, and "for almost all `n`" is
`Set.HasDensity … 1`.

The formalisation is by plby (github.com/plby/lean-proofs),
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos448.lean` together with the modules of
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos448/`. Those files are concatenated here in dependency order,
with their project-internal imports removed so that `Mathlib` is the only import, each
module's contents kept in a `section` carrying its own `open` lines, the whole wrapped once in
`namespace Erdos448`, the upstream trust-base print line and trailing `alias` removed, and the
final theorem renamed from `not_erdos_448` to `erdos_448`. No mathematical content is changed.
-/

